    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "# Sea Level Changes by Decade\r\n\r\nThe dataset contains monthly sea-level anomalies from New York’s East River. Grouping the data by decade can help reveal longer-term changes.\r\n\r\n`groupby('Decade')` organizes the rows into decade groups so `sum()` can calculate a total for each group.\r\n\r\n1. Complete the code using `groupby()` and `sum()` to calculate the total sea-level anomaly for each decade.\r\n2. Run the program and examine the results.\r\n3. Discuss which decades stand out and what the totals suggest about sea-level changes over time.\r\n4. Optional: Modify the code to calculate totals by year instead of decade.\r\n\r\n:::: details [Need Help?]\r\n\r\nAsk AI Tutor for an example of how `groupby()` and `sum()` work together, or ask it to explain the code, output, or documentation. Use its guidance to complete the work yourself.\r\n\r\n::::",
